From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 09:59:48 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] drm/sun4i: mixer: Set the mixer up again at mode set

sun8i_mixer_init() enables the mixer and sets the blender to its
defaults (background and bottom fill colour, blend mode of every pipe)
only when the mixer binds. Apart from the pipe control word, which the
plane commit writes, nothing writes them again. On the A733 the display
engine sits in the DE_SYS power domain, which genpd powers off in system
suspend. Without this, the display stays dark after resume, because the
DRM resume commits the planes, routes and mode again, but not the init.
Seen on the Radxa Cubie A7S: after s2idle the mixer enable and the
blender mode words read zero and the DisplayPort sink shows no picture.

Run the init from the mode_set callback of the engine, before the size
and interlace settings it already writes. The CRTC calls it from
mode_set_nofb when a commit changes the mode of an enabled CRTC, which
the atomic helpers do with the CRTC off; drm_atomic_helper_resume()
always does so, as the suspend left the CRTC disabled. The plane commit
that follows sets the routes and pipe enables again. Setting up the
global state of the display controller each time the CRTC is enabled is
what the Rockchip VOP2 driver does in vop2_enable(). It keeps the fix in
the driver that owns these registers. System sleep PM ops on the mixer
device would not do, because its driver data is set at bind and freed
with the bind resources at unbind. Apart from the pipe control word,
which the following plane commit rebuilds from all planes of the CRTC,
the init writes registers that only it writes, so on a display engine
that stays powered it repeats the values they already hold.

Not covered: the DE2 and DE3 registers the bind clears before the init.
The DE33 mixer of the A733 has no such step.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: after an s2idle cycle that powered the
DE_SYS domain off, the mixer enable and blender words read as before and
the sink saw the same picture again, second plane included.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun8i_mixer.c | 95 ++++++++++++++++-------------
 1 file changed, 51 insertions(+), 44 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun8i_mixer.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun8i_mixer.c
index a9549b530aa9..d973d56cbd11 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun8i_mixer.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun8i_mixer.c
@@ -381,6 +381,50 @@ static struct drm_plane **sun8i_layers_init(struct drm_device *drm,
 	return planes;
 }
 
+static void sun8i_mixer_init(struct sun8i_mixer *mixer)
+{
+	struct regmap *top_regs, *disp_regs;
+	unsigned int base = sun8i_blender_base(mixer);
+	int plane_cnt, i;
+
+	if (mixer->cfg->de_type == SUN8I_MIXER_DE33) {
+		top_regs = mixer->top_regs;
+		disp_regs = mixer->disp_regs;
+	} else {
+		top_regs = mixer->engine.regs;
+		disp_regs = mixer->engine.regs;
+	}
+
+	/* Enable the mixer */
+	regmap_write(top_regs, SUN8I_MIXER_GLOBAL_CTL,
+		     SUN8I_MIXER_GLOBAL_CTL_RT_EN);
+
+	if (mixer->cfg->de_type == SUN8I_MIXER_DE33)
+		regmap_write(top_regs, SUN50I_MIXER_GLOBAL_CLK, 1);
+
+	/* Set background color to black */
+	regmap_write(disp_regs, SUN8I_MIXER_BLEND_BKCOLOR(base),
+		     SUN8I_MIXER_BLEND_COLOR_BLACK);
+
+	/*
+	 * Set fill color of bottom plane to black. Generally not needed
+	 * except when VI plane is at bottom (zpos = 0) and enabled.
+	 */
+	regmap_write(disp_regs, SUN8I_MIXER_BLEND_PIPE_CTL(base),
+		     SUN8I_MIXER_BLEND_PIPE_CTL_FC_EN(0));
+	regmap_write(disp_regs, SUN8I_MIXER_BLEND_ATTR_FCOLOR(base, 0),
+		     SUN8I_MIXER_BLEND_COLOR_BLACK);
+
+	plane_cnt = mixer->cfg->vi_num + mixer->cfg->ui_num;
+	for (i = 0; i < plane_cnt; i++)
+		regmap_write(disp_regs,
+			     SUN8I_MIXER_BLEND_MODE(base, i),
+			     SUN8I_MIXER_BLEND_MODE_DEF);
+
+	regmap_update_bits(disp_regs, SUN8I_MIXER_BLEND_PIPE_CTL(base),
+			   SUN8I_MIXER_BLEND_PIPE_CTL_EN_MSK, 0);
+}
+
 static void sun8i_mixer_mode_set(struct sunxi_engine *engine,
 				 const struct drm_display_mode *mode)
 {
@@ -389,6 +433,13 @@ static void sun8i_mixer_mode_set(struct sunxi_engine *engine,
 	u32 bld_base, size, val;
 	bool interlaced;
 
+	/*
+	 * The display engine can lose its registers while the CRTC is off,
+	 * for example when its power domain goes off in system suspend, so
+	 * set the mixer up again before the new mode.
+	 */
+	sun8i_mixer_init(mixer);
+
 	bld_base = sun8i_blender_base(mixer);
 	bld_regs = sun8i_blender_regmap(mixer);
 	interlaced = !!(mode->flags & DRM_MODE_FLAG_INTERLACE);
@@ -466,50 +517,6 @@ static int sun8i_mixer_of_get_id(struct device_node *node)
 	return of_ep.id;
 }
 
